      </div>
      <main id="content"><h1>AffineGibbs: mathematical reading route</h1><p>Read the statements and derivations in source order. Every result has its own optional Lean statement and proof. Source assumptions, library reuse and unproved boundaries are kept explicit.</p><ol><li><a href="#decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs-map-affine-gibbs-afbd3acbfc">Actual affine normalized Gibbs transport</a></li></ol><section id="decl-autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs-map-affine-gibbs-afbd3acbfc"><article class="proof-reader" data-authored-declaration="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs"><div class="eyebrow">Samplinglib mathematical lesson</div><h2>Actual affine normalized Gibbs transport</h2><p><code>AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs</code> · theorem · <a href="index.html">Teaching coverage</a></p><section class="reader-first-pass" aria-label="First reading"><div class="reader-first-pass-label">Read this first</div><h3>Mathematical statement</h3><p class="reader-claim">The actual pushforward of the normalized Lebesgue Gibbs tilt under x-&gt;p+s*x is the normalized Lebesgue tilt with inverse-affine potential x-&gt;F(s^-1*(x-p)). The nonzero actual Lebesgue Jacobian cancels between partition and set numerator. This canonical identity alone makes no probability assertion.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation reader-main-equation">\[T(x)=p+sx,\quad H(x)=s^{-1}(x-p),\quad T_\#(Z_F^{-1}e^{-F}dx)=Z_{F\circ H}^{-1}e^{-F\circ H}dx.\]</div><h4>Proof roadmap</h4><ol class="proof-roadmap"><li><span>1</span><strong>Fix the true affine inverse</strong><p>Use T(x)=p+s*x and H(x)=s^-1*(x-p). Nonzero s gives H(T(x))=x and a measurable forward map, even for negative scales or zero dimension.</p></li><li><span>2</span><strong>Transform the actual Lebesgue integrals</strong><p>The canonical Haar scalar and translation change of variables applies to actual Bochner integrals. Apply it to exp(-F o H) and to its measurable-set indicator. Both the original partition and set numerator acquire the same real factor J; no moment or integrability estimate is assumed.</p></li><li><span>3</span><strong>Cancel the Jacobian in the normalized law</strong><p>Use map_apply on the measurable affine map and tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral on each measurable set. J!=0 cancels in the numerator/partition ratio. Mathlib totalizes improper integrals; this identity does not certify probability. The source consumer below derives positive integrability internally.</p></li></ol></section><details class="reader-ledger assumption-ledger"><summary>Full assumptions and notation</summary><h4>All objects and hypotheses</h4><ul><li>Finite real Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; any function F:E-&gt;R, any translation p:E and a real scale s!=0.</li><li>No continuity, measurability of F, exponential integrability, probability or moment premise. Equality is of Mathlib totalized normalized tilted measures; probability is a separate obligation for every consumer.</li></ul><p class="muted"></p></details><h3>Mathematical proof</h3><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>1. Fix the true affine inverse</h5><p>Use T(x)=p+s*x and H(x)=s^-1*(x-p). Nonzero s gives H(T(x))=x and a measurable forward map, even for negative scales or zero dimension.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[H(T(x))=x,\quad J=|s^{-d}|\ne0.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>map_affine_gibbs; Measurable.smul; smul_smul</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>2. Transform the actual Lebesgue integrals</h5><p>The canonical Haar scalar and translation change of variables applies to actual Bochner integrals. Apply it to exp(-F o H) and to its measurable-set indicator. Both the original partition and set numerator acquire the same real factor J; no moment or integrability estimate is assumed.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[Z_F=JZ_{F\circ H},\quad\int_{T^{-1}B}e^{-F}dx=J\int_Be^{-F\circ H}dx.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>Measure.integral_comp_smul; integral_add_left_eq_self; integral_indicator</p></details></div><div class="proof-reader-step"><h5>3. Cancel the Jacobian in the normalized law</h5><p>Use map_apply on the measurable affine map and tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral on each measurable set. J!=0 cancels in the numerator/partition ratio. Mathlib totalizes improper integrals; this identity does not certify probability. The source consumer below derives positive integrability internally.</p><div class="proof-reader-equation">\[\frac{J\int_Be^{-F\circ H}}{JZ_{F\circ H}}=\frac{\int_Be^{-F\circ H}}{Z_{F\circ H}}.\]</div><details><summary>Corresponding Lean step</summary><p>Measure.map_apply; tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral&#x27;; integral_div; mul_div_mul_left</p></details></div><section class="lean-verification"><h3>Lean verification</h3><p>The exact proposition and proof begin folded so the mathematical argument remains the primary reading path.</p><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-statement" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs"><summary>Lean statement · map_affine_gibbs</summary><p>The actual pushforward of the normalized Lebesgue Gibbs tilt under x-&gt;p+s*x is the normalized Lebesgue tilt with inverse-affine potential x-&gt;F(s^-1*(x-p)). The nonzero actual Lebesgue Jacobian cancels between partition and set numerator. This canonical identity alone makes no probability assertion.</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem map_affine_gibbs (F : E → ℝ) (p : E) {s : ℝ} (hs : s ≠ 0) :
    Measure.map (fun x : E =&gt; p+s • x)
      ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -F x)) =
      volume.tilted (fun x =&gt; -F (s⁻¹ • (x-p)))</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details><details class="inline-lean inline-lean-proof" data-inline-lean="AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs"><summary>Lean proof · map_affine_gibbs</summary><p>Fix the true affine inverse; Transform the actual Lebesgue integrals; Cancel the Jacobian in the normalized law</p><p>Braces mark parameters Lean can infer; square brackets request structures such as a measurable space or probability measure. Named hypotheses are mathematical premises, not facts established by this declaration. Section parameters are described in the mathematical hypotheses above; the module link retains their exact source context.</p><pre class="code-block"><code class="language-lean">theorem map_affine_gibbs (F : E → ℝ) (p : E) {s : ℝ} (hs : s ≠ 0) :
    Measure.map (fun x : E =&gt; p+s • x)
      ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x =&gt; -F x)) =
      volume.tilted (fun x =&gt; -F (s⁻¹ • (x-p))) := by
  let T := fun x : E =&gt; p+s • x
  let H := fun x : E =&gt; s⁻¹ • (x-p)
  let J : ℝ := |(s^Module.finrank ℝ E)⁻¹|
  have hJ : J ≠ 0 := abs_ne_zero.mpr (inv_ne_zero (pow_ne_zero _ hs))
  have hm : Measurable T := by dsimp [T]; fun_prop
  have hHT (x : E) : H (T x) = x := by simp [H,T,smul_smul,hs]
  have change_variables (f : E → ℝ) : (∫ x, f (T x)) = J*(∫ x, f x) := by
    have h := Measure.integral_comp_smul (volume : Measure E) (fun x =&gt; f (p+x)) s
    simpa only [integral_add_left_eq_self,smul_eq_mul,T,J] using h
  have hZ : (∫ x, Real.exp (-F x)) = J*(∫ x, Real.exp (-F (H x))) := by
    simpa only [hHT] using change_variables (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-F (H x)))
  ext B hB
  rw [Measure.map_apply hm hB,tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral&#x27; _ (hB.preimage hm),
    tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral&#x27; _ hB]
  congr 1
  rw [integral_div,integral_div]
  have hI : (∫ x in T ⁻¹&#x27; B, Real.exp (-F x)) =
      J*(∫ x in B, Real.exp (-F (H x))) := by
    have h := change_variables (B.indicator (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-F (H x))))
    have he : (fun x =&gt; B.indicator (fun y =&gt; Real.exp (-F (H y))) (T x)) =
        (T ⁻¹&#x27; B).indicator (fun x =&gt; Real.exp (-F x)) := by
      funext x
      by_cases hx : T x ∈ B &lt;;&gt; simp [Set.indicator,hx,hHT]
    rw [he,integral_indicator (hB.preimage hm),integral_indicator hB] at h
    exact h
  rw [hI,hZ]
  exact mul_div_mul_left _ _ hJ

end
end AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs</code></pre><p><a href="../modules/autosamplingtheory-technicallemmas-measure-affinegibbs.html#complete-module-source">Exact module and namespace context</a></p></details></section><details class="reader-ledger boundary-ledger"><summary>Scope and omitted-condition boundaries</summary><ul><li>Source realκ&gt;=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0&lt;eta&lt;=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta&lt;=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.</li></ul></details><details class="proof-reader-provenance reader-ledger"><summary>Sources, dependencies, and reuse</summary><h3>Source and reuse</h3><h4>Samplinglib parents called</h4><ul></ul><h4>Mathlib API called (external library)</h4><ul><li>Measure.integral_comp_smul</li><li>integral_add_left_eq_self</li><li>integral_indicator</li><li>Measure.map_apply</li><li>tilted_apply_eq_ofReal_integral&#x27;</li><li>mul_div_mul_left</li></ul><h4>Mathematical sources</h4><ul><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8">SPHMC Ex8/p4.2/p4.3 and scoped4.6; affine prerequisite</a> — Source realκ&gt;=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0&lt;eta&lt;=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta&lt;=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.</li></ul><p>Samplinglib prose is not a quotation or a source-equivalence certificate. Definitions and aliases are explained as constructions, not counted as new mathematical proofs.</p></details></article></section></main>
